<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.huffmanwrites.nord-stream-watch</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/bash</string>
    <string>/Users/prh/Developer/huffmanwrites/scripts/nord-stream-watch-runner.sh</string>
  </array>
  <!-- Watches for the two events that would change what "The Bet He Called a
       Fact" may say: a public reply from Jeffrey Sachs, and a verdict or new
       ruling in the Hamburg Nord Stream trial. Neither has a date, so nothing
       else in the pipeline can see either one.

       One fire a day at 09:15 CT, deliberately after the morning cluster: the
       daily SITREP publishes at 06:00 with its 07:00 watchdog, and this job
       competes with neither. It is a network read of two pages, so the exact
       minute does not matter; what matters is that it happens on a day nobody
       is looking.

       No RunAtLoad. A login is not a reason to check a news feed, and the
       checker writes nothing on a healthy run, so a load-time fire would only
       add noise to a log. The end date is the runner's guard, not the plist's:
       launchd cannot express one. -->
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <dict>
    <key>Hour</key>
    <integer>9</integer>
    <key>Minute</key>
    <integer>15</integer>
  </dict>
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>/Users/prh/Developer/huffmanwrites</string>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/prh/Library/Logs/nord-stream-watch.out.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/prh/Library/Logs/nord-stream-watch.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
